=== Vitamin D (25-OH Vitamin D)

Vitamin D deficiency is reported as highly prevalent in ME/CFS, attributed to activity limitations, indoor confinement, and sun avoidance. 25-OH vitamin D has immune-modulating effects mechanistically relevant to ME/CFS pathophysiology, including regulation of T-cell function and cytokine production. Standard thresholds apply: deficiency $lt$ 20 ng/mL, insufficiency 20--29 ng/mL. Correction of deficiency is recommended as standard of care.

⚠ *Contradicting evidence:* a direct cohort comparing ME/CFS (n=92) with controls (n=94) by LC-MS/MS found ME/CFS patients had *higher*, not lower, serum 25(OH)D (60.2 vs. 47.3 nmol/L, p=0.001), largely supplement-driven, with no association between vitamin D and fatigue severity @Earl2017VitaminD. That cohort was not severity-stratified, so whether the deficiency claim holds for the most housebound/very-severe patients (who plausibly have the least sunlight) remains an open question (@oq-vitamind-housebound). The evidence therefore does not support assuming deficiency a priori — a serum 25(OH)D measurement should guide supplementation.


